00:00:01.199 --> 00:00:02.629 align:start position:0%
 
well that was Graham Stewart a little  bit earlier on well joining me now is  the labor party chair annalize Dodds uh  very good morning to you thanks so much  for talking to us here this morning so  the government is deciding not to tell  people to cut their energy use this  winter they essentially say it's up to  them what does labor think  well actually we know that huge numbers  of people have already cut their energy  use I mean extraordinarily complacent I  have to say to hear some of this  discussion when already so many people  have been forced to drastically cut back  on their use of energy you know many  families expecting that they will only  be heating one room looking forward to  winter so that's already the reality for  many families and frankly this is a  damning indictment of conservative  policy over the last 12 years you know  we've not seen ultimately that gas  storage being open in fact a lot of it  has been closed During the period of  conservative-led governments we've not  seen the investment in Energy Efficiency  we've now got some of the coldest and  draftiest homes in all of Europe in our  country Libra's been calling for a mass  home insulation program no action it  seems being taken in that direction and  I'm afraid it's just not true for the  conservative government to say that we  have the right Energy Mix now we've seen  enormous delays on nuclear we've seen  huge blockages on homegrown Renewables  now that's why labors said we will be  sprinting ahead instead and why we'd  have GB energy to provide that green  cheaper energy for the future so you  know really this is an indication of  government failure that we're even  having these discussions right now about  potential blackouts but I just wanted to  ask you again about this question of  telling people to cut their own energy I  mean they would say they did say that  there's information out there on  official websites that you can get tips  on how to to save energy if you want to  but they say as far as energy security  is concerned it really wouldn't make  much difference  well actually improving the Energy  Efficiency of our homes would make a big  difference but that's not what it seems  the government is focused on they should  be focused on improving insulation for  example that would enable the creation  of jobs up and down our country's labor  has set out exactly how we would deliver  that in fact we've been calling for it  for a month upon month upon month and  still no action in the green homes grant  for example which was meant to be  improving the Energy Efficiency and  usage in British homes is a complete  failure and nothing's been done to  improve that situation so I think we  need to see action in that area but I do  think that the British public when so  many are already scaling back radically  on their energy use when they've been  forced to do that because of the  conservatives cost of living crisis as  well as the rising cost of energy I  think that would come across frankly as  very patronizing to those people  so what would labor do to ensure  stability of energy Supply and the  reason we're talking about this is  National Grid has said in the absolute  worst case scenario there may be the  prospect of planned blackouts in the  country what would labor do to ensure  stability of energy Supply in the short  term this winter next winter what would  they do  well the first thing we would do is that  mass home insulation program kirstema  called for that many many months ago  that should be taking place right now if  we'd acted on home insulation then the  very few poorest households would not be  as worried as they are right now about  the prospect of a cold winter secondly  we would be acting right now to improve  our energy Supply you know again care  set out in his speech at this conference  those measures up to 2030 some of them  to be taken very very speedily indeed to  be doing things like increasing those  homegrown Renewables you know we know  how to do this as a country just  yesterday in fact I was visiting a  facility where there's a huge enormous  battery going directly into the National  Grid but it's one of just a small number  of pilot projects you know the time for  Pilots is beyond us we should be acting  now and again Libra set out those plans  to act now and this is not only  important for our energy supply for  preventing these potential challenges  when it comes to blackouts it's also  very important for making sure our  country has those jobs of the future in  those green technologies in the future  and I'm afraid in both of those areas  the conservatives have failed while  labor has that plan that green  Prosperity plan to take our country  forward  but it's expensive isn't it I mean  Labor's talking about being an energy  superpower by 2030. I mean 28 billion  pounds each year  on this plan to boost Renewables and  Energy Efficiency how is that going to  be paid for  well actually it's very important that  we do that and if we don't it's going to  be more expensive in the future in terms  of that 28 billion pounds pledge we made  that some time ago we made that pledge  because ultimately unless we act the  costs for the future for our country  will be astronomical you know the um Obi  the independent fiscal Watchdog it's  made clear that if we put off this  action for another 10 years you know  we've had 12 years of drift if we put  off this action around the drive to Net  Zero for another 10 years they've said  it's going to be twice as expensive for  our country but also those renewable  Technologies are far cheaper when it  comes to energy it's far lower cost for  consumers that's why we should have been  acting over the last last 12 years we  haven't been labor set out that very  clear plan for us to make sure that we  get the benefit of those green  technologies you know our country she  can be a world leader in them we can  make up those 12 lost years if we have  that plan ultimately but we do need to  be acting on Energy Efficiency too and  that's why Labor's been calling for that  mass Homer insulation that's so  important and frankly if we don't do  these things the costs will just get  more and more for families and for  government okay I just want to ask you  about mortgage rates as well because  this week we've seen the average  two-year fixed rate mortgage rise to  over six percent for the first time  since 2008 what can be done to help  people  well the most important thing is that  ultimately economic credibility has got  to be re-established because ultimately  when we're seeing those increases in  mortgage rates that's been a direct  result from the conservatives mini  budget that they announced obviously  some time ago now labor said that the  government must come immediately back to  Parliament we've been calling for that  for some time now they need to reverse  that many budget it is ultimately the  cause of these increases  if you say that the mini budget is the  cause and unfunded tax cards why then is  labor adopting a lot of those tax cuts  well actually we're not we've got a  completely different approach when it  comes to fiscal policy compared with the  conservatives we've said that now is not  the time to be for example  yeah because if I've just finished I  mean that they're cutting tax on luxury  goods for tourists they're going ahead  of the corporation tax cuts you know  very very significant in terms of the  amount of money that that would raise  they've got a windfall tax that's full  of holes that isn't backdated in the way  that labor has called for and they're  also of course not releasing the obr's  analysis which has been provided to  government today which we believe  probably would show the negative  economic economic impact of all of these  tax cuts mainly for the wealthiest and  for profit-making companies and the  government's refusing to release that  analysis again if they did release it  that could increase confidence too and  help to get the cost of some of those  mortgages in the future at least down  the government is not acting to Inc  increase economic credibility it's labor  that's the party of economic credibility  and we need that change from the  conservatives as quickly as possible

